     "page": 1,
     "text": "Wilson-Johnson Medical Group\n\nRe: Sandra Martin (DOB 12/07/2005)\n\n---\n\nApril 11, 2025: Ms. Martin presented for her regularly scheduled follow-up visit regarding her atrial fibrillation/flutter. Her blood pressure at today’s visit was 134/80, and she weighed 183 pounds. She reports that she has been well overall. She is currently on amiodarone 200 mg daily, and her condition remains controlled. Her last echocardiogram was normal, and she has not had any episodes of atrial fibrillation/flutter since the last visit. \n\nOctober 15, 2024: Ms. Martin came in today for a follow-up regarding an upper respiratory infection (URI). Her blood pressure was and she weighed 177 pounds. She continues to manage her atrial fibrillation/flutter, which was diagnosed 3.4 years ago. Her condition remains stable, with a normal echocardiogram. She is currently taking amiodarone 200 mg daily. There have been no episodes of atrial fibrillation/flutter since her last visit.\n\nApril 19, 2024: Ms. Martin returned for a follow-up regarding her atrial fibrillation/flutter. Her blood pressure was 141/78, and she weighed 169 pounds. She reports feeling well overall. There have been no episodes of atrial fibrillation/flutter since her last visit. She is currently taking amiodarone 200 mg daily. Her last echocardiogram was normal, and she continues to be in a controlled state.\n\nOctober Z4, 2023: Ms. Martin visited today for a follow-up regarding her atrial fibrillation/flutter. Her blood pressure was 142/89, and she weighed 167 pounds. She has been doing well since her last visit. She is currently taking amiodarone 200 mg daily. Her last echocardiogram was normal, and she continues to be in a controlled state. This condition was diagnosed 3.4 years ago.\n\nApril 28, 2023: Ms. Martin was seen for a follow-up visit regarding her atrial fibrillation/flutter. Her blood pressure was 140/89, and she weighed 180 pounds. She reports feeling well overall. She is currently taking amiodarone 200 mg daily. There have been no episodes of atrial fibrillation/flutter since her last visit. Her last echocardiogram was normal.\n\nNovember 01, 2022: Ms. Martin visited today for a follow-up regarding her atrial fibrillation/flutter. Her blood pressure was 135/78, and she weighed 169 pounds. is currently taking amiodarone 200 mg daily. Her last was normal, and her atrial fibrillation/flutter has been controlled for years now. She continues to have no episodes of atrial fibrillation/flutter.\n\nMay 06, 2022: Ms. Martin came in today for a follow-up regarding an ankle sprain. Her"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "blood pressure was 141/80, and she weighed 179 pounds. She reports that the ankle sprain has healed well. She is currently taking amiodarone 200 mg daily to manage her atrial fibrillation/flutter, which was 3.4 years ago. Her last echocardiogram was normal, and she continues to be in a controlled state.\n\nNovember 09, 2021: Ms. Martin presented today for a follow-up regarding a back strain. Her blood pressure was 144/78, and she weighed 179 pounds. She reports feeling well overall. She is currently taking amiodarone 200 mg daily to manage her atrial fibrillation/flutter, which was diagnosed 3.4 years ago. Her last echocardiogram was normal, and she continues to be in a controlled state.\n\nMay 14, 2021: Ms. Martin visited today for a follow-up regarding her atrial fibrillation/flutter. Her blood pressure was 142/78, and she weighed 172 pounds. She is currently amiodarone 200 mg daily. Her last echocardiogram was normal, and her atrial fibrillation/flutter has been controlled for 3.4 years now. She continues to have no episodes of atrial fibrillation/flutter.\n\nAdditional Notes:\n\n- Ms. Martin exercises regularly, running 3-4 times a week.\n- She consumes approximately 8 alcoholic drinks per week.\n- Her father has type 2 diabetes, which was diagnosed he was 68 years old, and he is still living.\n\nSincerely,\nDr. David King\nCardiology\nWilson-Johnson Medical Group\n"
